# id  tag  kind  t_s  alt_km  L_si_W  flag  note
1 - first_light 0.0030 100.000 1.4303e+05 info  L_si first exceeds 1e-6 of its peak. This is just a visibility threshold; the real value depends on your sensor floor and on where the simulation starts (zstart).
2 A ablation_onset 0.9690 83.993 2.4811e+06 stylized  Net heating flux first exceeds radiative loss at T_ablate = 2300 K, so ablation switches on (a kink in the slope). Real onset is gradual over a few km. BELOW this point the model's light is drag work only (no ablated material): treat light above ~84 km as low-confidence. Loosely like the end of Phase 1 / start of Phase 2 in [R22], but the model has no spin, volatile (Na/K) emission or melt physics.
3 Y first_yield 3.2160 46.769 1.0217e+09 physical  Loading rho v^2 reaches S0 = 0.5 MPa. The body starts to flatten (pancake): area, drag and heating all grow, so the light rises faster. Analogue of the onset of fragmentation (Phase 5 / H_f in [R22]).
4 F flare 3.2824 45.671 3.0306e+09 stylized  Light rises x18.4 in 0.20 s (steeper than 3x the air-density tracking rate). Associated with: yield gen 0 at 46.7 km (99% of m0); split gen 0 at 44.8 km (99% of m0); yield gen 1 at 43.9 km (38% of m0). Dust groups supply 77% of the rise and 73% of the light at the end of the flare. A real fragmentation flare (Phase 5 in [R22]); its sharpness and timing here come from the model's deterministic cascade.
5 B first_breakup 3.3330 44.835 6.0373e+09 stylized  Spread factor reached f_split = 2: the body breaks into 4 children plus 20 % of its mass as dust. The dust has a large area-to-mass ratio, decelerates and ablates within a fraction of a second, which makes a sharp flare. The instantaneous release is a model simplification. Light grew x5.9 between first yield and this breakup (pancake spreading).
6 P peak 3.7660 37.858 7.2357e+10 physical  Maximum light. It sits ~+1.6 km from the peak of energy deposition (36.2 km) because the luminous efficiency tau(v) falls as the fragments slow (mass-weighted speed here 16.6 km/s).
7 b bump 3.7666 37.849 7.1866e+10 stylized  Small fluctuation, 29% above the local trend; coincides with a split (gen 2) at 37.7 km. The fine structure of this phase is set by the cascade rules, so its pattern is not predictive of a real event.
8 - drag_overtakes_ablation 3.9870 34.672 4.6072e+10 stylized  Drag work now exceeds the kinetic energy carried off by ablated mass. The ratio ablation/drag is about Lambda v^2/(2 Q Cd), so this happens when the speed falls below ~14 km/s (from the model's heating law).
9 D rolloff 4.1037 33.217 2.6577e+10 physical  Light has fallen to 1/e of the peak 0.34 s after it. Cause: the kinetic energy is being used up (speed 69% of v0, 43% of the mass still in flight) and tau(v) drops with speed. Analogue of Phase 7 (decline until dark flight) in [R22].
10 R retirement_step 4.8817 27.150 3.4129e+08 artifact  A group is removed because it slowed below v_dark = 3.0 km/s; the light drops 16% within 0.03 s. A bookkeeping step, not a physical dimming.
11 R retirement_step 4.9027 27.034 3.0073e+08 artifact  A group is removed because it slowed below v_dark = 3.0 km/s; the light drops 17% within 0.03 s. A bookkeeping step, not a physical dimming.
12 R retirement_step 4.9237 26.909 2.6476e+08 artifact  A group is removed because it slowed below v_dark = 3.0 km/s; the light drops 17% within 0.03 s. A bookkeeping step, not a physical dimming.
13 R retirement_step 4.9567 26.689 2.1627e+08 artifact  A group is removed because it slowed below v_dark = 3.0 km/s; the light drops 17% within 0.03 s. A bookkeeping step, not a physical dimming.
14 R retirement_step 4.9867 26.462 1.7943e+08 artifact  A group is removed because it slowed below v_dark = 3.0 km/s; the light drops 17% within 0.03 s. A bookkeeping step, not a physical dimming.
15 R retirement_step 5.0167 26.176 1.4836e+08 artifact  A group is removed because it slowed below v_dark = 3.0 km/s; the light drops 17% within 0.03 s. A bookkeeping step, not a physical dimming.
16 T tail 5.1247 25.484 7.2205e+07 low-confidence  Below 1e-3 of the peak the light is controlled by groups being retired when they slow below v_dark = 3.0 km/s and by the tau taper (2-4 km/s). Do not interpret structure below this level.
